From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:52:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 59/72] deepseek: fold wo_b's input rotation into wo_a's
 epilogue (TF_DSV41_ROT_FOLD=1)

With TF_DSV41_ROT_FOLD bit 0 set, wo_a's linear also writes wo_b's rotated
fp16 input rows: each warp's 128 output columns are rounded as the bf16
store rounds them, widened as rot_in reads them, then scaled by wo_b's suh,
transformed and stored exactly as seg_rot_in_kernel does. wo_b's rot_in
launch is dropped (one per layer per rank and round); L.oa is still written.
A layer keeps H's path unless every wo_a group's offset and width are
multiples of 128. Bits 1-2 are reserved for the attention and q-norm folds
and refused until built.

The fold runs new dense3 instances beside the existing linear; unset or 0
emits what H emits and does not resolve them. Host tests cover the knob,
the emitted windows on and off, and a bitwise twin of the rotation path;
`tf-dsv41-test rot-fold` compares the bytes on a GPU.

Mechanism after Bertholomus's dsv41 grouped-linear RotOut fold
(exl3_linear.zig, round.zig), re-implemented here; credited in docs/credits.md.

Co-authored-by: bertholomus <311723197+bertholomus@users.noreply.github.com>
